---
const steps = [
	{ id: "01", name: "Intake", skill: "issue-intake", state: "stable" },
	{ id: "02", name: "Contract", skill: "Issue Contract", state: "artifact" },
	{ id: "03", name: "Shape", skill: "solution-gate", state: "stable" },
	{ id: "04", name: "Change", skill: "implementation", state: "work" },
	{ id: "05", name: "Prove", skill: "test-strength", state: "experimental" },
	{ id: "06", name: "Review", skill: "review-gate", state: "evaluated" },
	{ id: "07", name: "Record", skill: "record-a-case", state: "stable" },
];
---

<section id="workflow" class="workflow section-shell" aria-labelledby="workflow-title">
	<div class="section-heading">
		<div>
			<p class="eyebrow">Workflow</p>
			<h2 id="workflow-title">A factory loop, not a prompt collection.</h2>
		</div>
		<p>Enter at the earliest incomplete state. Open work can hand off and re-enter.</p>
	</div>

	<div class="workflow-board" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Engineering workflow, scroll horizontally to inspect every step">
		<ol class="workflow-steps">
			{steps.map((step) => (
				<li>
					<span class="step-index">{step.id}</span>
					<div><strong>{step.name}</strong><code>{step.skill}</code></div>
					<small>{step.state}</small><span class="step-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
				</li>
			))}
		</ol>
		<div class="handoff-loop">
			<strong>Cycle open?</strong><code>handoff → workstream-reconcile → Change</code>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>
